# Handover sign-in returns to the trip: Google sign-in from the full sign-in page keeps the return path, and the trip page opens the modal on an expired token. Issue 2865, root cause on the issue. Tier A (identity). 2026-09-15
#
# DISPATCH: ./scripts/dispatch.sh git@github.com:Arlencho/olympus-platform.git wave-plans/assistant-channel/2026-09-15-handover-signin-return.plan --detach --retries 1
# TIER: A
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1 | web-frontend | Branch fix/handover-signin-return from origin/main. Read issue 2865 and its root-cause comment first. ONE, apps/web/app/auth/page.tsx: before GoogleSignInButton navigates, write the olympus_auth_return_to sessionStorage hint from the redirect query, accepting only a same-origin path that starts with a single slash (never an absolute URL, never a protocol-relative path, never a backslash), exactly as components/auth-modal.tsx does; apply the same to any other sign-in method on that page that leaves the page. TWO, apps/web/app/r/[id]/atlas-result-session-page.tsx and apps/web/lib/api-client.ts: the trip fetch of the handover page handles its own 401, including a request that carried an expired token, by clearing the dead token and opening the in-page sign-in modal over the mounted trip shell (the existing requestAuthForExpiredSession path), never the global bounce to the sign-in page; every other page keeps the global session-expiry behaviour. No new copy. Tests: Google sign-in started from the sign-in page with a redirect to a trip returns to that trip; an absolute or protocol-relative redirect is ignored and falls back to the start page; an expired token on an assistant trip opens the modal and never navigates to the sign-in page; after the modal sign-in the trip hydrates with its option selected; the global bounce still happens on another page. VERIFY: web unit tests for the touched files, web lint and web typecheck, real exit codes in the PR body. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Open a draft PR with Closes 2865 and Refs 2800. | fix/handover-signin-return

2 | frontend-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of the PR on branch fix/handover-signin-return. Tier A, round 1 of at most 4. No commits, no push, no review, no labels; tmp writes only. Record head SHA at start and at report. Walk the real paths: expired token on an assistant trip link, signed-out visitor, sign-in by code, magic link and Google from both the modal and the full sign-in page; each must land on the trip with the option selected. Confirm other pages still get the global expiry bounce. Post ONE comment on issue 2340 whose first line reads FRONTEND CRITIC HANDOVER SIGNIN RETURN with SAFE-TO-MERGE, BLOCK-FIX or BLOCK-ESCALATE and citations. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash, no AI tool or vendor name. | fix/handover-signin-return

2 | security-reviewer | SECURITY REVIEW of the PR on branch fix/handover-signin-return. Read-only; tmp writes only. Record head SHA at start and at report. The change writes a return path from a URL query into sessionStorage and follows it after sign-in. Check for open redirect (absolute, protocol-relative, backslash, encoded and javascript URLs), that the hint is cleared after use, and that the handover 401 handling never leaks trip data before access succeeds. Post ONE comment on issue 2340 whose first line reads SECURITY HANDOVER SIGNIN RETURN with a final SAFE or BLOCK line. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash, no AI tool or vendor name. | fix/handover-signin-return
